= January 2020 — The first opposition succession

At the campaign opening, **Grzegorz Schetyna** still led Civic Platform. Two
national defeats made his control the question in a direct membership ballot.
He stood aside for Tomasz Siemoniak; members instead gave **Borys Budka** a
first-round mandate and asked a younger parliamentary camp to renew KO without
dismantling its alliance.

Budka may work with us on courts and elections, but he will compete harder for
urban professionals and younger anti-PiS voters. We need a relationship with
his new leadership, not a celebration of somebody else's succession.

- @budka_social
- @budka_democratic
- @budka_compete

@budka_social
title: Offer Budka a joint social-opposition working group
subtitle: A practical opening on households and work; Razem fears liberal dilution.
on-arrival: ko_leadership_response_2020 = "Joint social-opposition working group"; ko_relation += 5; household_policy_pressure += 2; labor_credibility += 2; razem_dissent += 3; last_policy_stage = "Joint opposition proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Lewica and KO party leaderships"; last_policy_implementation = "Not enacted"; news_headline = "Budka receives a concrete social-cooperation offer from Lewica"

Budka accepts a table on household security and work. We gain a channel into
KO's new executive; Razem watches for the moment cooperation becomes dilution.

- @po_handoff_continue: Continue to the campaign ecosystem

@budka_democratic
