@ko_candidate_replacement_2020
# prose-audit: Grade A — KO's candidate reset is narrated as a direct threat to Lewica, with political subtitles and authored consequences.
title: [? if pres_2020_ko_kidawa: Kidawa-Błońska stays on the ballot?][? if not pres_2020_ko_kidawa: Kidawa-Błońska withdraws; Trzaskowski takes the ballot?]
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 32
order: 18
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2020 and month = 5 and ko_candidate_replacement_2020_done = 0
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kidawa.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.ko_candidate_replacement_2020_done = 1;
Q.ko_presidential_outgoing_2020 = "Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska";
// KO's swap was an internal decision taken under pressure, not a certainty. A
// party whose boycott line has been vindicated, or one that still trusts the
// primary it ran, can leave its original nominee in place.
const kidawaStaysRoll = this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
const kidawaStaysChance =
    0.22 +
    (Q.postal_election_stance == "Boycott" ? 0.26 : 0) +
    ((Number(Q.ko_relation) || 50) >= 60 ? 0.06 : 0);
Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa = kidawaStaysRoll < kidawaStaysChance ? 1 : 0;
Q.ko_presidential_candidate_2020 = Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa
    ? "Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska"
    : "Rafał Trzaskowski";
Q.pres_2020_ko_name = Q.ko_presidential_candidate_2020;
Q.pres_2020_ko_surname = Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa
    ? "Kidawa-Błońska"
    : "Trzaskowski";
Q.ko_candidate_incoming_bloc = Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa
    ? "the primary electorate, Budka's reluctant executive and the parliamentary old guard"
    : "Budka's executive, KO's allied parties and the metropolitan local-government wing";
Q.ko_poll_momentum += Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa ? -1.8 : 2.5;
Q.ko_coalition_dissent += Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa ? 5 : 2;
Q.news_headline = Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa
    ? "Kidawa-Błońska refuses to withdraw and KO enters the reset campaign with its primary winner"
    : "Kidawa-Błońska withdraws and KO unanimously turns to Rafał Trzaskowski";
!}

= May 2020 — A candidate collapses with the election calendar

**Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska** won KO's primary, then called for a boycott of an
improvised May vote that never happened. Weeks without a settled ballot drove
her campaign to the edge of viability.

[? if not pres_2020_ko_kidawa: She withdraws; Budka's executive and every KO
partner turn to Warsaw mayor **Rafał Trzaskowski**, who can collect signatures
and attention before the reset campaign is over.?][? if pres_2020_ko_kidawa:
She does not withdraw. The executive cannot agree on a replacement quickly
enough to matter, the mayors who wanted Trzaskowski are told that overturning a
primary in June would cost more than losing with its winner, and KO enters the
rescheduled campaign behind a candidate polling in single figures.?]

[? if not pres_2020_ko_kidawa: The replacement closes our easiest route into the
runoff and gives progressive voters a much stronger rival. Trzaskowski may still
be the partner against Duda in July, but we should decide the price before KO's
relaunch consumes the field.?][? if pres_2020_ko_kidawa: That leaves the largest
anti-PiS electorate in the country attached to a candidacy that cannot reach the
runoff. It will look for somewhere else to go in the next six weeks, and every
campaign in the field — including ours — is now competing for it.?]

- @kidawa_rules
- @kidawa_terms
- @kidawa_compete

@kidawa_rules
